Yeeeeesss. Please get Hatoful Boyfrieend. ;_;
There are so many great things aside from the whole "you're a human dating birbs" thing. As you play through the routes, eventually you realize that the routes connect to each other in a way to create a singular story and the game manages to keep you interested the whole time and wonder what's going to happen next. There's a lot more underneath the surface of the game that you won't expect, so this is definitely not something you should judge solely on the cover.
This game is basically brilliant and you should be playing it right now!!!

Playing this game wasn't a horrible experiece, but wasn't a good one eighter.
The only really good thing I can say about it is that it really captures the spirit of the Cold War times.
-Buggy: at least 3 times I had to reload a chackpoint because the trigger wouldn't kick in;
-Bad save system based on checkpoints;
-Moral decision have almost null impact in the game (even at the ending where it SEEMS to change something). The truth is that this is a linear "on the tracks game" masked as more free decision thing.
-There is very low customization options and there is no effort to create an emotional attachment with the characters;
-The IA is pretty terrible, forcing you in some parts to to lower the game difficulty to get past them;
-The user IA is REALLY terrible;
-Combat is clumsy  (this one is hard to explain, the best way to say it is that in Mass Effect, running and shooting is much more "fluid" than in The Bureau XCOM;
-Short list of sidequest with little to no meaning.
I could list some other things. I admit it, maybe I placed the bets to high in this game expecting it to be like Mass Effect or XCOM - Enemy Unknown. But the truth is that this seems like a game that tried to much stuff for the budget they had and at the end we have only a superficial experience of what this "stuff" could really have been.

So guys, here is a honnest guy from a player that plays evolve since his early stages in 2015:
I have to admit that i was a fanboy of the old Evolve, and quite the kind of guy ho buys every DLC just for supporting the developers of the game i most enjoyed that time, thats totally fine and i encourage you all to do it with your favourite games, but the point is that besides me and some more veterans of Evolve, people didnt wanted to spend their money everytime a new hunter/monster/skin was added, so they quit the game, now the game came back with a few differences:
-At the moment the game is 100% free to play, including all characters, skins, maps and perks;
-Thoose ho bought the game early will now have founder status;
-Founders have special badge items and can keep everything they had for free (without having to spend the ingame currency);
-The game is no longer a full realease and its now on its BETA phase;
-The game was modded to have a shorter ingame time and a more friendly experience to new players (no more cloaking(exept for lazarus), all hunters can dome without failing the dome, trapper's new class abillity is a radar that tells the general location of the monster, wildlife is slighty weaker so that both monster and hunters can proceed their chasing quicker, etc...);
-All the stats have been reseted ( elite skins, accolades, achievements...);
-They plan to add a new character every 2 weeks;
-Turtlerock has been very responsive in forums and has updated the game alot more freequently now.
AFTER ALL GIVE IT A TRY ;)

